cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bytery: A Schema-Aware Binary Serialization Protocol"
message: "If you use Bytery, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Porciuncula da Silva"
    given-names: "Jackson"

repository-code: "https://github.com/jacksonsolid/Bytery"
url: "https://github.com/jacksonsolid/Bytery"
abstract: >
  Bytery is a schema-aware binary serialization protocol designed as a compact
  and efficient alternative to JSON for transport and storage scenarios. It uses
  a structured binary wire format with schema tables, string tables, date tables,
  compact integer encodings, null-aware primitive encodings, and optional outer
  GZIP compression.

keywords:
  - serialization
  - binary protocol
  - JSON
  - codec
  - schema-aware encoding
  - wire format
  - compression
  - data transport

license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-03-01"